{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem U2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>The following problem is from the Ultimate Question of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a>, where solving this problem required the answer of a previous problem. When the problem is rewritten, the T-value is substituted.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f76e209ba6efb92105415d4f3c62ef804a52519d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is right. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b36b86ac878ee1b707085fe4ae5a913e78e631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d99eb629f027ee953f4fce4c24425c6fb800a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 5$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/05415b5dfc4a5f716b14abe2488fe7b4d8a2faa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 6$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />. Determine the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5fa2b4aca7257e2460e27a4910f42731cbc3fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACDB$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abee71171256aa5b98954710a59865eb1b5dac8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),10)); draw((0,10)--(0,0)--(10,0)--(0,10)); draw((0,3)--(4,0)); label(&quot;O&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;C&quot;,(0,3),W); label(&quot;A&quot;,(0,10),N); label(&quot;D&quot;,(4,0),S); label(&quot;B&quot;,(10,0),E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. The radius of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/9013d89763ccd1def6bfbbb1f4d94c49f58a31ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, so the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff1d53900652da5f2d40ef5427512642e85c0b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e7a76e5e433a2e9a1a996406fb3506c115e70c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^2 + (x+1)^2 &amp;= 25 \\\\ x^2 + x^2 + 2x + 1 &amp;= 25 \\\\ 2x^2 + 2x - 24 &amp;= 0 \\\\ x^2 + x - 12 &amp;= 0 \\\\ (x+4)(x-3) &amp;= 0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"172\" height=\"127\" />\nSince lengths must be positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> equals the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd97737c9a1eb5146725902d4e4c4bda1388129b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> minus the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4097e707215c7c2085c3fd539de4c228d44f1880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09c6ac154d72c2040848be7f2868bab2441e8e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCD] = \\tfrac12 \\cdot 10^2 - \\tfrac12 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = \\boxed{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"273\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem U1\">Problem U1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problem U2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem